<title>ITALY: RAS says 1996 parent net profit up 6.1 pct.</title>
<headline>RAS says 1996 parent net profit up 6.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian insurance company RAS saw its 1996 parent net profit rise 6.1 percent to 338 billion lire from 1995, but it left its 1996 ordinary share dividend unchanged at 340 lire, said a statement from the group on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The company added that it had increased its stake in Italian banking group Credito Italiano to five percent, and that it had also held its 1996 dividend on its savings shares at 400 lire per share.</p>
</text>
